  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European-Israeli-Palestinian trilateral dialogue 2024-26</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: European-Israeli-Palestinian trilateral dialogue 2024-26 - The brutal and indiscriminate terrorist attack by Hamas across Israel on 7 October 2023, and the large-scale Israeli military operation on Gaza thereafter, has and is resulting in unprecedented levels of violence, trauma and destruction. The voices in favour of peace, reconciliation and accountability, whether in the Occupied Palestinian Territories, in Israel or globally, are being drowned by hostile and violent narratives, and by the continued hostilities, the spill-over risks of which cannot be undermined. It is urgent to continue supporting the voices and actions in favour of peace, including civil society initiatives, as an integral part of any viable process to end the Israeli/Palestinian conflict. The meaningful relationships and initiatives of and between Palestinian and Israeli civil society actors that had once provided pathways for peace at a societal level, are all the more important at this juncture, in parallel to diplomatic efforts. The objective of the action is therefore to enhance the global role of civil society in advocating for lasting peace between Palestinians and Israelis through support to civil society in their efforts for sustainable peace.</narrative>
  </description>
